<title>USA: SPC cuts U.S. posted crude prices 25 cts/bbl.</title>
<headline>SPC cuts U.S. posted crude prices 25 cts/bbl.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Scurlock Permian said it cut the price it will pay for U.S. crude oil by 25 cents a barrel, effective today.</p>
<p>The decrease brings the new price for U.S. benchmark grade West Texas Intermediate to $23.75 a barrel, and West Texas Sour to $21.50 a barrel.</p>
<p>Light Louisiana sweet crude is now $23.75 a barrel, and Oklahoma sweet is $23.75.</p>
<p>Scurlock Permian is a subsidiary of Ashland Inc.</p>
<p>-- New York Energy Desk, +1 212 859-1620</p>
</text>
